{
  "tema": 8890,
  "slug": "preposicion-que",
  "titulo": "Asking questions with preposition + qué",
  "subtitulo": "¿Para qué? ¿Con qué? ¿De qué hablas?",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "In Spanish the preposition goes at the start of the question, before qué: ¿De qué hablas? (What are you talking about?). Never leave it at the end like in English.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In English the preposition often ends the question: _What are you talking **about**?_ In Spanish that's impossible. The preposition goes **first**, right before **qué**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "¿",
            "preposition + qué",
            "+ verb...?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Many verbs come with a preposition (**hablar de**, **pensar en**, **referirse a**, **soñar con**), and it moves to the front with them."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Qué** keeps its accent: it's a question word."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: in Spanish the preposition never gets left at the end of the line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿==Para qué== me llamaste?",
              "en": "What did you call me for?"
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==En qué== ciudad estás?",
              "en": "Which city are you in?"
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==De qué== querías hablar conmigo?",
              "en": "What did you want to talk to me about?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No te entiendo… ¿==a qué== te refieres?",
              "en": "I don't understand… what do you mean?"
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿==Con qué== lo hiciste? —Con plastilina.",
              "en": "—What did you make it with? —With modeling clay."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==En qué== estás pensando?",
              "en": "What are you thinking about?"
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Por qué== lo dices?",
              "en": "Why do you say that?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Qué estás ahorrando para?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿Para qué estás ahorrando?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Qué hablas de?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿De qué hablas?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Con que lo pagaste?"
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿Con qué lo pagaste?"
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Don't forget the accent."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
